This was my second ascension in the last week. I got a priest out 
earlier and, while deciding what kind of character I would ascend next, 
decided to play a wizard for fun since I like wizards. The results were 
better than expected.

I started out life with a sleep spell and the usual force bolt spell. 
For kicks, I thought, hey, why not see if I can get to minetown as a 
level 1 wizard and boost my AC early. So I let my pet kill everything in 
sight and went to the mines early. Along the way, I found a fairly large 
hardware shop on lvl 3 of the main dungeon with a magic lamp and a magic 
whistle. I grabbed the stuff and headed down.

Sadly, I didn't get there as a level 1 wizard but I did arrive in one 
piece. I found a potion of holy water in the deli, id'ed it on the 
altar, blessed my lamp and got a wish (+2 silver dragon scale mail). 
Once my pet killed half the guards and given the altar was not 
coaligned, I opted to take my pet and head back to the main dungeon.

By that time, I had used tripe rations to enlist several other pets, 
including a large dog. A bones file later on produced a number of 
spellbooks and water potions. Life started getting easier when I found 
some speed boots in a shop.

I thought about completing Sokoban but that seemed boring. So I kept 
going down, and down, and down. I didn't mean to take it that far, but I 
wound up digging down to the castle, where I wasted the guards and 
grabbed the WoW on the level. I restrained myself from going nuts 
wishing for stuff, since I still hadn't completed either the mines or 
Sokoban. I did, however, wish for a magic marker, which I used to write 
a spellbook of identify. I id'ed my stuff and went back up, getting a 
bag of holding in Sokoban and the luckstone out of the mines. I amassed 
sufficient power to dump the pets, nurse dance, and enter the quest at 
level 17. The dark one never knew what hit him.

My stupid god, however, would not crown me, no matter how many corpses I 
sacrificed on an altar on level 20. I really wanted a SoFD, but didn't 
want to wish for one. With a ring of slow digestion in my inventory I 
wasn't in a hurry, so I went into Gehennom full blast.

Who knows why my God got angry, but he did, and I lost all the AC I had 
gotten from bribing the priests. I had reached Rodney's tower and 
figured I'd try to get crowned. I got nuked on my AC instead. Stupid 
god. Well, -32 AC would just have to do.

I did, however, find yet another WoW in the tower. So I got my spellbook 
by wishing. It came in handy when I used it to wish for a c corpse right 
before facing Orcus. No need to let him call upon big meenies like 
Demogorgon or Yeenoghu (or both).

In hindsight, I suppose it would have been beneficial to genocide 
liches, but I never did. They hounded me the whole game but did no real 
damage. I easily offed Rodney and the High Priest in short order and 
headed out. Rodney is always a barrel of laughs; he appears at opportune 
moments talking trash, only to get instadeathed. Funny!

I used the very last charges of my last WoW to get some potions of 
confusion so I could easily locate the portals with some gold detection 
scrolls I saved up. I also saved up wands of teleportation for the 
astral plane - they came in handy. While they don't work well on the 
riders, they work on everyone else. The altar was in the middle and was 
the 2nd altar I tried.

